From e1377cfde25c63337d03cf92e7a9d2bc55ee1744 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:37:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] session: run without systemd (elogind's sd-bus, no
 --systemd off systemd)

DEsk already worked without libsystemd, but a machine that runs elogind
instead of systemd (s6, OpenRC, runit) lost the post box, the tray, MPRIS
and power-off through logind, and was told at every login that systemd
"said no".

- meson: sd-bus comes from libsystemd or, failing that, libelogind, which
  installs the same <systemd/sd-bus.h>. -Dpost works on elogind.
- session.c: `dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd` and
  `systemctl --user unset-environment` only where systemd is init
  (/run/systemd/system, what sd_booted() asks); elsewhere the D-Bus update
  alone, which is all there is to update.
- power.c: without sd-bus, power off and restart through loginctl
  (systemd's or elogind's) before systemctl.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
